# Pairs with OnlySupersededRefused. A refused claim stops the activation even
# while its row still holds its own write, instead of bumping above the refusal
# and claiming again. Another leaf's retirement then deactivates a live leaf
# whose claim was in flight (#5635), and a restart can stop the current one.
MODULE: OnlySupersededRefusedRefuseWithoutBump
TARGET: OnlySupersededRefused
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: every claim refusal stops the activation, whether or not its row holds
PERTURBS: ClaimRefuse

--- FIND
    /\ Refused(a)
    /\ ~CanBump(a)
--- REPLACE
    /\ Refused(a)
\* MUTATION: no bump; a refusal always stops.
--- END
